  "term": "filter",
  "definition": "In this context, a filter is something used to reduce or modify incoming light so visual comfort can be improved and discomfort from glare can be limited. The source supports this meaning specifically in relation to matching light filters to a person’s sensitivity and outdoor lighting conditions.",
